hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1066","Abu Bakr said: I had dictated at the beginning of the book the news of Talha bin Ubaid Allah on the issue of the Bedouins, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Islam, and the Prophet’s response, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Five prayers per day and night,” so he said: Do I have to do anything else? He said: “No, unless you do it voluntarily.” Then the Prophet, the Chosen One, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught that any prayer that exceeds five prayers is voluntary."
"1067","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, and Muhammad bin Hisham told us: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us. Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, said: Ali said: The Witr prayer is not obligatory, nor are your obligatory prayers, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, performed the Witr prayer, then he said: “O people of the Qur’an, perform the Witr prayer, for God is the Witr prayer and loves the Witr prayer.” However, Al-Ashjaj did not mention: O people of the Qur’an, perform Witr. Muhammad bin Hisham said, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, and Sa`id bin Abdul Rahman al-Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, about The hadith of Al-Dawraqi in its chain of transmission, and its text"
"1068","Bundar told us, Abdullah bin Hamran told us, Abdul Hamid bin Ja’far bin Abdullah told us, Ja’far bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amra al-Najjari, who asked Ubadah ibn al-Samit about the Witr prayer, said: “It is a good and beautiful thing that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did.” “peace be upon him and the Muslims after him, but it is not obligatory.” Abu Bakr said: I included in the book of Al-Kabir the narrations of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his announcement that God had enjoined upon him and his nation five daily prayers. Today and tonight, these reports indicate that the obligation of performing the Witr prayer is obligatory for the servants, requiring them to perform six prayers a day. And tonight, this article is contrary to the narrations of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and contrary to what the Muslims understand, their scholar and the ignorant among them, and contrary to What do the women in the chamberlains, the boys in the chambers, the male and female slaves understand, when they all know that the obligatory prayer is five, not six?"
"1069","Ayoub bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abd al-Warith bin Saeed, who said: I asked Abu Hanifa, or Abu Hanifa was asked, about Witr prayer. He said: An obligatory prayer. I said: Or he was asked: How much is the obligatory prayer? He said: Five prayers. Then he was asked: What do you say in Witr prayer? He said: An obligatory prayer. So I said, or it was said to him: “You are not good at calculating.”"
